course: dictionary
lesson: 15855
title: Unfasten and undo
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To unfasten something means to open it or undo it. You can unfasten a button, a buckle, a belt, a clasp or a lock. «Mia unfastened her coat because the room was warm.» Her coat was done up, and now it is open.
explain: Unfasten can also mean to come undone by itself. «The strap unfastened and the bag slid off her shoulder.» Nobody pulled the strap. It simply came loose. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning is used.
explain: Notice the un- at the start of unfasten. It usually turns an action around, so fasten means to close or join, and unfasten means to undo that. When you meet a word with un-, ask whether the meaning is the opposite of the word without it.
fact: Unfasten means to open something that was fastened, or to come undone by itself.
fact: Unfasten is a verb: unfasten, unfastens, unfastened, unfastening.
fact: You can unfasten a button, buckle, belt, clasp or lock.
fact: Safety rule: never unfasten your seat belt while the car or plane is moving. Wait until the seat belt sign is off.
fact: A good check is to swap in «undo» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Ben unfastened the buckle on his sandals.» What does unfastened mean? | Tightened very hard | Cleaned carefully | *Opened or undid | Lost forever
exercise: «The strap unfastened and the bag slid off her shoulder.» What does this show? | Somebody pulled the bag | Nothing happened | *The strap came undone by itself | The strap was made of metal
exercise: When should you unfasten your seat belt on a plane? | Before the plane takes off | While the plane is moving | *After the seat belt sign is switched off | Whenever you feel a bit bored
test: Which of these can you unfasten? | The sky | A cloud | A song | *A buckle
test: «Dad said, "Wait until the sign goes off before you unfasten your seat belt."» Why does he say this? | Because seat belts are only for sleeping | To keep the seat belt clean | *Because it is not safe to unfasten it while the vehicle may be moving | To make the seat belt tighter
exam: Dana says unfasten means to tie something tighter. Is she right? | No, it means to paint something | Yes, it means to tie something tighter | *No, it means to open or undo | Yes, it means to lose something
